Task: Fix postal code validation in ExtractOfOwnersFilterSection.tsx
The current validation hardcodes postal codes to exactly 5 digits, which incorrectly rejects valid codes from most countries. This project targets Schengen, EU, and Nordic countries, and the "Country of residence/registration" section allows multi-select. Please implement country-aware, multi-country postal code validation as follows.
1. Create a postal code pattern map (new file postalCodePatterns.ts or top of component):
Typescript
2. Update validatePostAddress to accept an array of country codes (multi-select support):
Typescript
3. Wire up country selection state:
When "Select all" (countries) is chosen → pass undefined/empty array to validatePostAddress → uses DEFAULT fallback.
When "Select the countries" is chosen with one or more countries picked → pass the array of ISO codes (e.g. ["SE", "NL", "PL"]).
A postal code is valid if it matches any of the selected countries' patterns.
4. Fix range (From/To) validation:
Remove all hardcoded length === 5, /^\d{5}$/, or digit-only checks anywhere in the Post Address section (including "Range of post addresses" and single "Post addresses" fields).
Validate both From and To individually via validatePostAddress(value, countryCodes).
Only enable "Add to selection" when both From and To pass validation.
Handle the case where From and To might match different countries' formats within the same selected set — this should still be considered valid as long as each individually matches at least one selected country's pattern.
Handle edge cases: empty string, whitespace-only input, leading/trailing spaces (trim before validating), lowercase letters in alphanumeric codes (e.g. Latvia/Lithuania/Malta — validation should be case-insensitive).
5. Update error/help messages dynamically:
Single country selected: show format hint, e.g. "Format: 1234 AB (Netherlands)".
Multiple countries selected: on failure, show "This postal code doesn't match any of the selected countries' formats."
No country selected (Select all): "Enter a valid postal code."
Keep the existing "Add at least one postal code range" message for the empty-range case, but remove any message implying a fixed digit count.
6. Regression check:
Search the whole file (and any shared validation utils it imports) for other places that assume 5-digit postal codes and update them consistently.
Confirm no other component reuses the old single-string signature of validatePostAddress — update all call sites to pass an array.
7. Add/update unit tests covering:
Sweden: 123 45 (valid), 12345 (invalid — needs space per pattern, confirm intended strictness)
Netherlands: 1234 AB (valid), 1234AB (valid per pattern), 12345 (invalid)
Poland: 12-345 (valid), 12345 (invalid per pattern, confirm intended strictness)
Finland: 12345 (valid)
Latvia: LV-1010 and lv1010 (both valid, case-insensitive)
Malta: ABC 1234 (valid)
Multi-country selection ["SE", "NL", "PL"]: code 1234 AB valid (matches NL), code ABCDE invalid (matches none)
No country selected: generic alphanumeric 2–10 chars accepted, e.g. AB123
Empty/whitespace input: invalid
Run npm run lint after changes and fix any resulting lint errors.
